---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, apps, href } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Support" description="Get help or share an idea.">
  <section class="wrap section narrow">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="lead">Something not working, or an idea to make an app better? We read everything.</p>
    <p><a class="btn primary" href={site.contactHref}>Email {site.contactEmail}</a></p>
    <p class="muted">Tell us which app, what device and browser you are using, and what you expected to happen. A screenshot helps.</p>

    <h2>Quick answers</h2>
    <h3>Where can I use the apps?</h3>
    <p>The web versions are for testing and trying things out, in any modern browser on your phone, tablet or computer. What you enter there is not kept, and there is no sign-in or syncing. The iPhone, iPad and Android apps, which are where your information is kept, are coming to the Apple App Store and Google Play.</p>
    <h3>Why can't I find the app in the App Store or Google Play?</h3>
    <p>The store versions are not listed yet. Until they are, you can try the web version from its page on this site. It is for testing.</p>
    <h3>Will it work without internet?</h3>
    <p>The iPhone, iPad and Android apps do: your information is saved on the device, and syncs when you are back online. The web test versions need a connection.</p>
    <h3>I used the web version and my information is gone.</h3>
    <p>The web versions are for testing only and do not keep what you enter: it is gone when you close or reload the page. Use the iPhone, iPad or Android app for anything you want to keep.</p>
    <h3>An app shows an old version.</h3>
    <p>On the web, reload the page. On iPhone, iPad or Android, update the app from the store.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
